{#
    FR-029 — visible on every page while a Super Admin is viewing the platform as someone else.

    Included from both template roots (base.html.twig and videos/base.html.twig) rather than
    injected by a response listener, so it is markup in a layout and not HTML assembled in the
    HTTP layer.

    `IS_IMPERSONATOR` is Symfony's own attribute for "this token is a switched one", so the
    banner cannot disagree with the firewall about whether a switch is active.

    Accessibility: role="status" announces it without stealing focus, and the state is carried
    by the words "Viewing as" as well as by the colour — colour alone would say nothing to a
    screen reader or to a red-green colour-blind operator (NFR-X04, NFR-023).
#}
{% if is_granted('IS_IMPERSONATOR') %}
    <div class="impersonation-banner" role="status">
        <strong>Viewing as {{ app.user.displayName }}</strong>
        <span>({{ app.user.email }})</span>
        <a href="{{ path('admin_impersonation_exit') }}">Exit impersonation</a>
    </div>
    <style>
        .impersonation-banner {
            position: sticky;
            top: 0;
            z-index: 1000;
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: .75rem;
            align-items: center;
            padding: .6rem 1rem;
            background: #b91c1c;
            color: #fff;
            font: 500 .95rem/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif;
        }

        .impersonation-banner a {
            margin-left: auto;
            color: #fff;
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        .impersonation-banner a:focus-visible {
            outline: 3px solid #fff;
            outline-offset: 2px;
        }
    </style>
{% endif %}
